{
    "background_story": "Malia was a talented artist who saw the world in a unique way. Born with tritanopia, a rare form of color blindness that affects the perception of blue and yellow hues, she had learned to adapt and find beauty in the world around her. As a child, Malia struggled to distinguish between certain colors, but as she grew older, she discovered that her condition allowed her to see subtle nuances in shades and textures that others often missed. She developed a distinctive art style that emphasized contrast and tone, creating stunning pieces that seemed to pulse with energy. Malia's tritanopia became a defining aspect of her art, and she found solace in the fact that her unique perspective allowed her to bring a fresh vision to the world of art.",
